+# Complete recompose after sports-rock rejection
+
+Owner reports menu cracks in the Windows game, then: "Also the music is a bit
+annoying, it doesn't really match 'more sporty and energetic,' and 'the ability
+to build athmosphere similar to the music from Ori games'. The Ori and the blind
+forest has excellent soundtrack and we must match the quality, but the style
+and tempo needs to be right for a racing game. You need to completely recompose
+the music"
+
+Sports-rock-2026-10-08 is rejected for musical fit/irritation. Broad recompose is
+authorized; previous motif/parts are unapproved and may be replaced. Keep the
+background purpose, confidence-based progression, one-minute exceptional payoff,
+looping, five related palettes, silent hover and persisted levels. No physics,
+camera, backend or vehicle-SFX changes.
+
+Hypothesis: short repeated programmed riffs and sharp percussion cannot provide
+the requested phrase development and atmosphere. Explore two new original
+performed cinematic/rock cues with longer phrases, melodic bass, agile drums,
+strings/piano and gentler attacks. Target160BPM. Referenced games are artistic
+quality/atmosphere direction; no copied recordings, melodies or conditioning.
+
+Existing local Magenta RT2 is verified before use; no hosted generation or new
+runtime dependencies. Complete generated mixes are labelled as such. Any derived
+runtime parts must share one source performance and verified clock, and must not
+be described as isolated instruments without actual separation evidence.
+
+The preserved menu master/decoded/Godot mixer capture has no large discontinuity
+at its34.286s wrap. The strongest repeating sample differences are hat attacks
+within each bar. Full Windows menu capture records two natural wraps/four
+navigations. These are technical findings, not proof of what the owner heard;
+the new score must include repeated full-menu playback checks.
+
+Raw sources and the rejected bank remain preserved. Owner listening, natural
+driving and device/audio-route acceptance are unverified; no AAA claim.
